  "result": "I fixed the open-bound clamping bug in `IntRange`. Values outside the range now clamp to the first allowed value inside it.\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. Previously, `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-1` returned `-1`, and the max-open case moved the wrong way too.\n- **Tests:** I added two cases to `tests/test_types.py` next to the existing clamp cases:\n  - `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"-1\"` returns `1`.\n  - `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"9\"` returns `4`.\n- **Results:** `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py` gives 71 passed, 2 skipped.\n\nI didn't commit anything, since you didn't ask for a commit.",
